.TH szip 1 "July 2026" "szip 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\fBszip\fR \- Advanced adaptive multi-stage compressor with neural modeling
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBszip\fR \-c \fIinput\fR \fIoutput.sz\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
\fBszip\fR \-d \fIinput.sz\fR \fIoutput\fR
.br
\fBszip\fR \-i \fIinput.sz\fR
.br
\fBszip\fR \-Ev \fIinput\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBszip\fR is an extremely powerful, adaptive compressor designed to squeeze out maximum redundancy by employing a dynamic combination of algorithms. 
Unlike static compressors like gzip or xz, \fBszip\fR automatically chunks the input data into independent blocks using entropy variance (Content-Defined Chunking), and evaluates multiple algorithmic pipelines (BWT, RLE, MTF, LZ77, Neural Arithmetic Coding) on the fly to select the globally optimal compression chain for each specific block.
.PP
If a directory is provided as input, \fBszip\fR will automatically package it using \fBtar\fR prior to compression, and seamlessly extract it upon decompression.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-compress\fR \fIinput\fR \fIoutput.sz\fR
Compress a file or directory into a .sz archive.
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-decompress\fR \fIinput.sz\fR \fIoutput\fR
Decompress a .sz archive to the specified output file or directory.
.TP
\fB\-i, \-\-info\fR \fIinput.sz\fR
Print internal block structure and pipeline metadata of a compressed archive without decompressing.
.TP
\fB\-Ev, \-\-eval\fR \fIinput\fR
Evaluate the input data by running a brute-force sweep in memory, and print ONLY the optimal entropy threshold integer to standard output. Excellent for automation scripts.
.TP
\fB\-a, \-\-adaptive\fR
Enable block-level adaptive algorithm selection (default).
.TP
\fB\-b, \-\-block\-size\fR \fIKB\fR
Maximum block size limit in KB. Default is 16384 (16MB). For massive files, higher limits allow the LZ77 engine's VarInt window to find extremely distant redundancy, at the cost of higher RAM usage.
.TP
\fB\-e, \-\-entropy\fR \fITHRESHOLD\fR
Specify the exact entropy-boundary sensitivity for block chunking (default: 200). A higher value merges blocks together, favoring huge LZ77 dictionaries. A lower value fractures heterogeneous files into smaller, purer blocks, preserving local dictionaries.
.TP
\fB\-E, \-\-auto\-entropy\fR
Enable dynamic entropy auto-tuning based on exponential variance. The compressor will react strictly to local entropy shifts to sever blocks at data-type boundaries.
.TP
\fB\-Ea, \-\-brute\-force\fR
Sweep a comprehensive range of entropy thresholds in memory to locate the absolute global optimum for the file's chunking strategy, ensuring maximum possible compression ratio.
.TP
\fB\-t, \-\-threads\fR \fINUM\fR
Number of threads to use. By default (0), it automatically scales to the number of logical cores.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Compress a directory with maximum brute-force optimization:
szip \-c ./my_project release.sz \-Ea
.TP
Quietly find the best entropy threshold for a mixed binary:
BEST=$(szip \-Ev firmware.bin)
.br
szip \-c firmware.bin firmware.sz \-e $BEST
.TP
Extract an archive quickly using all CPU cores:
szip \-d dataset.sz dataset_extracted \-t 0
